## Coralogix clarifies Events2Metrics cardinality-overflow behavior

Source: Coralogix — https://coralogix.com/docs/user-guides/release-notes/metrics/
Published: 2026-10-12
Channel: news

The Metrics release notes clarify that when a rule reaches its cardinality limit, overflow label values are aggregated under `CoralogixOtherValues`; the documentation change does not describe dropping all subsequent measurements. It also documents the organization-level quota behavior for new or edited rules.

Why it matters: That distinction matters during incident diagnosis: an overflow bucket signals cardinality pressure, but it is not the same failure mode as ingestion stopping.

## Google SecOps adds Response Health Hub for playbook operations

Source: Google Cloud — https://docs.cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/secops/release-notes
Published: 2026-10-12
Channel: news

Google SecOps release notes list the Response Health Hub on October 12, giving operators a place to inspect response/playbook health and related operational signals. This is security-automation operations visibility, adjacent to core infrastructure observability.

