## DigitalOcean launches a managed data layer for agent context and execution traces

Source: DigitalOcean — https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/introducing-agent-data-services
Published: 2026-10-12
Channel: news

Agent Data Services entered private preview as a managed catalog for multimodal content, structured records, and agent sessions. The announcement describes capturing execution traces and feeding session state into retrieval and evaluation workflows over time.

Why it matters: It treats agent histories as durable operational data, though private preview is not a generally available service and its capabilities need hands-on validation.

## Splunk argues agent risk needs runtime observability and controls

Source: Splunk — https://www.splunk.com/en_us/blog/observability/rapidly-control-ai-agent-risk-before-it-hits-the-business.html
Published: 2026-10-12
Channel: news

Splunk's post connects agent behavior and tool-call visibility with security controls, arguing that an agent can complete a technically valid action while still producing an unacceptable business outcome. It positions runtime observation alongside prevention and policy enforcement.

Why it matters: Operational success needs more than uptime and latency: teams need to inspect what the agent decided, what tools it used, and whether the outcome was acceptable.

## Vibe-coded infrastructure still needs production-grade observability

Source: Splunk — https://www.splunk.com/en_us/blog/observability/vibe-coded-infrastructure-is-still-infrastructure.html
Published: 2026-10-12
Channel: news

Splunk's engineering post makes the case that infrastructure generated with coding agents remains production infrastructure: it still needs testing, ownership, security controls, and telemetry after deployment. The useful shift is to treat generated changes as software changes, not as disposable prompts.

Why it matters: If an agent can create or modify infrastructure, observability and change accountability need to cover the generated artifacts and their runtime effects.

## Elastic Agent Builder adds shared conversations for team handoffs

Source: Elastic Search Labs — https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/agent-builder-conversation-sharing
Published: 2026-10-12
Channel: news

Elastic announced shared conversations in Agent Builder so teams can hand an agent session to colleagues with its prior context intact. The article describes availability on Elastic Cloud Serverless first, with other deployment options on a separate rollout path.

Why it matters: This is useful for investigation handoffs, but shared conversation history is not a substitute for trace-level observability or audit evidence.
